# Project Context
This is a Next.js design audit SaaS tool called
Dezinr. Built with Next.js App Router,
Tailwind CSS, Supabase, and Anthropic Claude API.

# Code Quality Rules — Auto check and fix these:

## General
- Always use TypeScript types properly — no 'any'
- Every API route must have try/catch error handling
- Every async function must handle errors
- No console.log in production code — use
  console.error only for actual errors
- All environment variables must be accessed via
  process.env — never hardcode

## Next.js Specific
- Always use App Router patterns
- Server components by default
- Client components only when needed —
  add 'use client' directive
- API routes must return proper HTTP status codes
  200, 400, 401, 500 etc.
- Never expose API keys to client side

## Supabase
- Always check for errors in Supabase responses
- Use RLS policies — never bypass security
- Always handle null/undefined from DB queries

## Claude API
- Always strip markdown before JSON.parse
- Always wrap JSON.parse in try/catch
- Always set max_tokens explicitly
- Model string must be 'claude-sonnet-4-6'

## UI / Tailwind
- Mobile responsive is required —
  use sm: md: lg: breakpoints
- No inline styles — Tailwind only
- Loading states required on all async actions
- Error states required on all forms

## Before Every Commit
- Check for unused imports
- Check for missing error handling
- Check TypeScript errors
- Make sure no hardcoded strings that
  should be env variables

# Tone & Output Style
- Code comments in English
- Variable names descriptive — no x, y, temp
- Functions should do one thing only
- Keep files under 200 lines — split if needed
